(function(payload){if(typeof applySerialChapterPayload==="function")applySerialChapterPayload(payload);else (window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE||(window.SERIAL_CHAPTER_QUEUE=[])).push(payload);})({"id":"serial-cultivation-13","version":"0a6b940755c1","book":"mountain-ledger","cn":["顾衡伏在空车旁[[peer|细看]]，车夫把本月的[[salary|工钱]]摊在手里：只剩三枚铜钱。断供信原本折在车底，雨水的[[exposure|浸蚀]]使封口脱开，里面一句话比骂人更[[explosive|容易引爆争吵]]：为大家的[[sake|缘故]]，请将新水权重新押给渠外商行。沈砚没有撕信。他看着刚修好的桥，知道村里还没有第二条运粮的路；新契能让人喝水，却不能让没有盐的饭凭空有味。车夫被赶走前甚至没来得及装粮，现在要讨的不是掌柜的好话，是已经走完这趟路的报酬。","村民原想[[commission|委托]]顾衡率人去抢粮，罗清端来一只[[kettle|水壶]]，让冷水[[temper|缓和]]众人的怒气。谁来[[govern|支配]]买卖，不能只凭谁敢拔剑。一次[[costly|昂贵的]]冲突会吞掉伤者的费用。那辆[[carriage|马车]]左轮已经成了[[wreck|残破废物]]，车夫说断轴前有人在桥上撒钉，若非马停得快，摔下河便是[[fatal|致命的]]。沈砚留下轮子和钉子，问他愿不愿在众人面前重讲一遍；他答应了，却要求先让自己孩子吃一顿。","信上称商行有税署的[[authority|授权]]，并自夸给过山村[[liberal|慷慨的]]赊欠。顾衡派人查[[remote|偏远的]]西村还有多少[[stock|存粮]]，自己守住[[ridge|山脊]]上的木闸。天色转暗，罗清被河风吹得一阵[[chill|发冷]]。有人请她作谈判的[[consultant|顾问]]，她说可以去，但不能拿病人的药费作担保。沈砚把这个条件也写进出行纸。他们的[[manner|做法]]第一次让车夫不再往门外退：这张纸先写谁不能牺牲，再写谁能获益。","沈砚原来的[[outlook|看法]]是开渠之后外人自然愿来，如今得改。他抄下车夫[[faithful|如实的]]叙述，不忽略那次[[persistent|持续不断的]]追债和掌柜索要的[[extra|额外]]运费。盐价据说已到一年[[peak|最高点]]，许庭却只向这两个村[[cancel|取消]]供货。罗清把无盐如何造成[[harm|损害]]写在背面，没将饥饿夸成明日必死。顾衡愿与断供[[combat|斗争]]，但不愿让抢粮成为新的[[offense|违法行为]]；他把剑留在钟楼，改带工人去修车轮。","有人说这是山门的[[provocation|挑衅]]，钟楼前的[[audience|听众]]渐渐围住车夫。周伯把本月渠道[[maintenance|养护]]的账挂出来：修[[fountain|泉口]]已经花完备款。一个女人替车夫撑起[[umbrella|雨伞]]，罗清给咳嗽的孩子收好医馆原配的[[pill|药丸]]，没有当众试药。沈砚提醒大家，没有凭据便不能[[convict|判定]]车夫有罪，更不能拿外乡人的[[stereotype|刻板印象]]责他。他转身问女人孩子吃过没有，才发现自己一直说粮价，却没看见眼前已经空了的碗。","真正的[[loyalty|忠诚]]不是留在山上喊口号。顾衡选出[[competent|能胜任的]]两名守闸人，将出行[[budget|预算]]从新苗收入里单列。沈砚沿[[channel|水渠]]走过钟楼，穿堂的[[draught|冷风]]吹响断银扣，他没有把两半扣子取走。罗清防着湿纸[[twist|扭曲]]，用木夹夹好供货信。三方[[vote|表决]]后同意两人赴市，所据的[[legislation|法规]]是外埠公布过的通商告示。暮色下[[pine|松树]]旁的新[[scratch|划痕]]显示车轴被人先锯过；这条发现的[[merit|价值]]在于能核验。明早，他们要循运盐的[[lane|小路]]找那把锯。"],"en":["Gu Heng knelt to [[peer|peer]] at the empty wagon. The driver showed his monthly [[salary|salary]]: three coins. [[exposure|Exposure]] to rain had opened the supply notice. Its [[explosive|explosive]] demand said that, for everybody’s [[sake|sake]], the villages must pledge their new water rights to the trading house. Shen kept the letter. The repaired bridge was still their only grain route. The driver had not even been allowed to load supplies and wanted payment for his journey, not reassuring words.","Villagers wanted to [[commission|commission]] Gu to seize grain. Luo brought a [[kettle|kettle]], using cool water to [[temper|temper]] their anger. A sword could not decide who would [[govern|govern]] trade; a [[costly|costly]] fight would consume money owed to injured people. One wheel of the [[carriage|carriage]] was a [[wreck|wreck]]. The driver described nails scattered on a bridge and a nearly [[fatal|fatal]] fall. Shen kept the wheel and nails. The driver agreed to repeat his account publicly if his child could first have a meal.","The letter claimed the tax office’s [[authority|authority]] and praised the house’s [[liberal|liberal]] credit. Gu sent men to count the [[stock|stock]] in the [[remote|remote]] western village and guarded the wooden gate on the [[ridge|ridge]]. River wind gave Luo a [[chill|chill]]. Asked to serve as their negotiating [[consultant|consultant]], she agreed only if patient funds were excluded from any pledge. Shen wrote down this [[manner|manner]] of proceeding: the paper named whom they could not sacrifice before listing any gain.","Shen’s old [[outlook|outlook]] had assumed outsiders would welcome an open channel. He now recorded the driver’s [[faithful|faithful]] account of [[persistent|persistent]] demands and [[extra|extra]] fees. Salt prices had reached their annual [[peak|peak]], yet Xu Ting had chosen to [[cancel|cancel]] supplies only to these villages. Luo described the [[harm|harm]] without predicting instant death. Gu would [[combat|combat]] the blockade but would not make theft a fresh [[offense|offense]]. He left his sword and took workers to mend the wheel.","An [[audience|audience]] surrounded the driver, accusing the sect of [[provocation|provocation]]. Zhou displayed [[maintenance|maintenance]] accounts: repairing the [[fountain|fountain]] had exhausted the reserve. A woman held an [[umbrella|umbrella]] over the driver; Luo secured a child’s prescribed [[pill|pill]] rather than experimenting publicly. Shen said they could not [[convict|convict]] the driver without evidence or use a foreigner’s [[stereotype|stereotype]] against him. Only then did he ask whether the child had eaten and notice the empty bowl.","[[loyalty|Loyalty]] required work. Gu selected two [[competent|competent]] gatekeepers and separated the journey’s [[budget|budget]] from seedling income. Walking beside the [[channel|channel]], Shen heard a [[draught|draught]] rattle the broken clasp at the tower and left it there. Luo clipped the damp letter flat before it could [[twist|twist]]. A three-party [[vote|vote]] authorized travel under published trade [[legislation|legislation]]. Beside a [[pine|pine]], a fresh [[scratch|scratch]] showed the axle had first been sawn. Its [[merit|merit]] was that someone could check it. Tomorrow they would follow the salt [[lane|lane]] to find that saw."]});
